#lego-legacy-route 1
# Hot Wheels Stunt Track Driver, from its boot through its first race to the
# finish, and out on Escape (#89).
#
# The maintainer's own play, recorded from the window. Mattel Media's splash
# fades up from flip 101 and semi logic's follows it; the intro starts at
# about 260, and Space at 285 skips it to the main menu. The click at 625 is
# on the crossed flags, bottom right, which open the track select; the one at
# 748 is its green arrow, taking the first track. On the car select the click
# at 837 is on the wheel and the one at 870 its green arrow, which starts the
# race.
#
# The starting line is up from flip 872, the car dropped onto it. Its lights
# come on red from 960 and go green by 1000, with Up revved before them and
# held from 988; by 1020 the car is away. The arrows steer it round the house,
# and at about 3300 it goes through the hoop into the television with the
# clock stopped at 1:19. The finish plays out on the screen, and the results
# are up by 3730, the race's best time written to saves\times.dat just before.
# Escape at 3900 is this title's quit, and the run ends three flips later.
#
# The play began from the maintainer's saves, whose wheel had a car on the
# spoke the click at 837 lands on. Every replay starts from a machine with
# nothing saved, so it races the car the select opens on instead, and the
# flips above are that race's: it finishes all the same.
